          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observed, from the port breakwater, two bright lights stacked vertically. The lights moved erratically and were joined by several others. The witness thought it might be a release of lanterns. The observation of orange lights in the sky in less than a minute, following the same trajectory, on a weekend night, strongly suggests Thai lanterns, likely released nearby after a private party. The lights were moving from North to South (towards the sea). The wind in Nice was light, nearly zero. (see weather). The local wind is a very unpredictable local breeze. Due to the witness's description, which matches the Thai lanterns in every way, the GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\", a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
